rac{5}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=-2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b7c0e75-3d49-5406-9041-ede1d5bfdf47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351962} {:answer/id #uuid "33bb1eb5-07b0-5c72-9e4a-a39b341c088c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352048} {:answer/id #uuid "6b960fbb-7fd4-564b-88d9-596a86197fe5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352519} {:answer/id #uuid "a471234f-1f9f-56ed-9886-d314b4205faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352971} {:answer/id #uuid "e3378a1b-e1c9-5e1d-b90b-a6157d273dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351962} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba728d29-f974-5f4e-bf33-9c1c26f466d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354136}] :question/id #uuid "83ac805a-2248-5c38-94ec-8370eb490b39" :question/math-academy-id "q-85928" :question/problem "Given that $\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{A}^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-7A+8I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-7A+8I) & =O \\\\ A-7I+8{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{7}{8}I-\\frac{1}{8}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{7}{8},$ $q=-\\frac{1}{8}$ and\n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{7}{8}+(-\\frac{1}{8})=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354447 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fb6cd75-1b66-5eef-bdd2-d1c1efa8bd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351849} {:answer/id #uuid "3110eedf-37d2-5058-a8cb-2890631cedaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352019} {:answer/id #uuid "50826028-f314-5a71-8097-5a7dc84cf792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49I-12A+{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352291} {:answer/id #uuid "b3125bf0-b9d9-57a1-9d2f-231388faed3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353099} {:answer/id #uuid "dca93f44-d070-505c-ab70-65f10c6983ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9I+2A+{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353488}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353099} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec8c9dce-00e3-5b5f-901c-e3b2b9cd794b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354221}] :question/id #uuid "cddc84f4-8d27-54c1-a11e-f66ad824ed8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-85929" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((5-\\lambda )^{2}+4) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +29) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+12{\\lambda }^{2}-49\\lambda +58 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+12{A}^{2}-49A+58I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+12A-49I+58{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{58}(49I-12A+{A}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373778 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65f78fe5-8a0b-5c8c-9ba2-f234eec8b977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373780} {:answer/id #uuid "51d79449-387a-514d-b3bd-9b95e771984f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373781} {:answer/id #uuid "22be24f4-9f88-5ef3-8ae7-2e85d07ed518" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373782} {:answer/id #uuid "84d983e6-6863-5892-b6cf-e9c5d7dfb428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373783} {:answer/id #uuid "de911146-38f6-5073-bdea-99b438169ff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373780} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fff8c60-4f3f-55de-8054-ba67d1fcd863" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373779}] :question/id #uuid "6944e235-260f-5526-a1a0-03870ed7a8fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-140534" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and ${A}^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value of $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )+12 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +22 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-7A+22I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-7A+22I) & =O \\\\ A-7I+22{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{7}{22}I-\\frac{1}{22}A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=\\frac{7}{22},$ $q=-\\frac{1}{22},$ and \n\n$$\np+q=\\frac{7}{22}+(-\\frac{1}{22})=\\frac{3}{11}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186430412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054199c2-5c89-5ffd-aead-8b50d8e9a898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430393} {:answer/id #uuid "10181856-84b4-5e5e-8832-61fff9b19f1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}A+\\frac{3}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430394} {:answer/id #uuid "87762782-8da5-5b58-aec6-89ebd72a1767" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430401} {:answer/id #uuid "8e1bad79-e653-5c1b-8674-be7f593dc2d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}I-\\frac{5}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430402} {:answer/id #uuid "97594f4f-bc35-5637-b1b2-7a025224b4ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2}I+\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430393} :answer-field/id #uuid "34db680c-e9af-57f5-a298-893f9c03dc9c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186430408}] :question/id #uuid "8f9a6384-39b0-554b-abeb-cd550f81dcbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-85930" :question/problem "If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},$ then ${A}^{-1}=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )+2) & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+5\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{A}^{3}+5A-2I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}(-{A}^{3}+5A-2I) & =O \\\\ -{A}^{2}+5I-2{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ 2{A}^{-1} & =5I-{A}^{2} \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =\\frac{5}{2}I-\\frac{1}{2}{A}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing the Inverse of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Its Powers"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124537 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124346 :question/id #uuid "8e6d3017-d05d-5a2d-8043-c827e612476e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5511" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\textrm{tr}(A)=-4$ and $\\textrm{det}(A)=-18.$ If $A^2 = xA + yI$ for constants $x$ and $y,$ then find the value of $x+y.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda)=\\lambda^2-\\textrm{tr}(A)\\lambda+\\textrm{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-4A+18I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x+y = -4+18 = 14.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2867571-c1ae-5ea0-b784-22f444c8db38" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eeaeba1-c3f6-5a7d-a932-2a93d587aa08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8A-12I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324111} {:answer/id #uuid "93630f9d-78cf-5ded-84e9-aa19f6f346a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8A-12I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325225} {:answer/id #uuid "d767c0ea-0291-536a-9373-acea6eed3f45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8A+12I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325844} {:answer/id #uuid "e13638e9-fd7d-54e3-b7c7-c72968ee0f67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A-8I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325943} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d1e6eb-8e9b-5cb4-b09a-3fd437a73eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A+8I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8A-12I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325225} :answer-field/id #uuid "d94788c2-43f9-5632-900c-78fd51b91761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326614}] :question/id #uuid "56a1bd4c-16fb-5242-9ca4-9449cd0cb6e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-38702" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\text{tr}(A)=-8$ and $\\text{det}(A)=12.$ Then, ${A}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =-8A-12I.\