#edb/ref 17592186430409}] :question/id #uuid "ad99eb94-2179-5889-bd75-4a31770a9b01" :question/math-academy-id "q-83394" :question/problem "Let $A$ be a $2\\times 2$ matrix such that $\\text{tr}(A)=5$ and $\\text{det}(A)=9.$ Then, ${A}^{2}=$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by \n\n$$\np(\\lambda )={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(A) & =O \\\\ {A}^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)A+\\text{det}(A)I & =O \\\\ {A}^{2} & =\\text{tr}(A)A-\\text{det}(A)I \\\\ {A}^{2} & =5A-9I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Power of a Matrix as a Linear Combination of Smaller Powers"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124538 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124347 :question/id #uuid "ce724b3b-f440-5c1f-86a6-c50a54931233" :question/math-academy-id "e-5512" :question/problem "Given that ![](images/bd/bdf92550ba4b8fa58da146c944a99a57e35e13e4885c3a2309ab291a4a4177e4.svg) and $f(x) = x^{12} -x^{10} +2x-1,$ find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & -5 \\\\ 3 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )+15 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\:\\:x^{10}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x^2-1\\:$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\!\\require{enclose}\\enclose{longdiv}{x^{12} \\, - \\, x^{10}  +  2x  -  1 {\\phantom{|}} }$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x^{12}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x^{10}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$1$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{10}({x}^{2}-1)+(2x-1),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x) = x^{10}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A) = q(A)p(A)+(2A-I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(2A-I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(2A-I) \\\\  & =2A-I \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -5 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -10 \\\\ 6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0247d89f-77e8-54f5-b78f-f2c7b483b0ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A-4I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440847} {:answer/id #uuid "0343e746-54c1-5222-a796-90c29e7ea995" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6A-7I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440848} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3df907-a08f-519e-85c3-b63849202be3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5A+3I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440849} {:answer/id #uuid "2c07895d-da5f-54b1-bff6-0d6c2e69c22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5A+6I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440850} {:answer/id #uuid "c633453c-2299-56d8-9764-d824d1d6ce62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A+4I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5A+6I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440850} :answer-field/id #uuid "9684056b-e027-57d4-8919-30e81288ed74" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123176}] :question/id #uuid "08bd910e-aeba-525b-9826-35ee9b3eaf71" :question/math-academy-id "q-37775" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+x-2,$ then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{4}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+x-2,$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}+x-2\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"9\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{4}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{4}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$5x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$6$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{4}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4} & =q(x)p(x)+(-5x+6),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{2}-x+3.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=q(A)p(A)+(-5A+6I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & =q(A)p(A)+(-5A+6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-5A+6I) \\\\  & =-5A+6I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125106 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "834aa185-6012-5fad-9cec-bfae8e36cc07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392142} {:answer/id #uuid "ba614c81-25e5-56b2-a980-247e1c339a6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392143} {:answer/id #uuid "9f8f194b-9c47-54bc-9f21-95b6a53aec45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392144} {:answer/id #uuid "30a72e6d-1f6b-54c6-a30e-be3b5a7ecb69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392145} {:answer/id #uuid "918cb8aa-dfd0-58f5-94c4-133741fe2164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392145} :answer-field/id #uuid "8edebb12-abdf-545c-97fb-264d8989834b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392141}] :question/id #uuid "9892d6a4-00e5-53a4-a283-14b8510646e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37835" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $\\,f(x)={x}^{22}-{x}^{20}+3x-2\\,$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )+8 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{20}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-1\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{22}\\,-\\,{x}^{20}\\,+\\,3x\\,-\\,2\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{22}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{20}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(3x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{20}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(3A-2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(3A-2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(3A-2I) \\\\  & =3A-2I \\\\  & =3\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -9\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -6 \\\\ 12 & -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272142 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025a5c1a-4f6e-5e42-8dce-96a2fd08178a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & -42 \\\\ 14 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269289} {:answer/id #uuid "23310913-8cd2-557c-be76-7e2691fe0ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}31 & 14 \\\\ 42 & -25\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269575} {:answer/id #uuid "9142a6e7-f5cb-5d0d-bcaf-2c7c6f384044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 14 \\\\ -42 & 30\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270533} {:answer/id #uuid "efb97e7a-5224-5bc1-9035-2d0d54445cd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 12 \\\\ -24 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271376} {:answer/id #uuid "f7416ab1-633c-5a86-bade-cffdf59d2d02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 14 \\\\ -42 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271438}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 14 \\\\ -42 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271438} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d72f403-dcf6-5b06-9505-8ae246f18a3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271759}] :question/id #uuid "af2db92b-ede0-52d7-a7d4-1043a63d9db0" :question/math-academy-id "q-140602" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $\\,f(x)={x}^{16}-4{x}^{14}+7x-3\\,$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )+12 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{14}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-4\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{16}\\,-\\,4{x}^{14}\\,+\\,7x\\,-\\,3\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{16}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{14}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$7x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(7x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{14}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(7A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(7A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(7A-3I) \\\\  & =7A-3I \\\\  & =7\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -6 & -4\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 & 14 \\\\ -42 & -28\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 14 \\\\ -42 & -31\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272144 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e162e3d-1633-55b7-8ea0-da3f552cfce0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21A+2I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269520} {:answer/id #uuid "5c4a988e-1c9e-5ee9-8dfd-776fb2e04770" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-10A+7I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270093} {:answer/id #uuid "5f6dd8fb-7d08-5fd3-992e-5b662e3d7b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39A+22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270115} {:answer/id #uuid "82601323-a446-5473-8e90-7d849e426742" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30A+15I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270396} {:answer/id #uuid "dfdca89a-ab25-5510-937d-af0b09efe13a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12A+53I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-39A+22I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270115} :answer-field/id #uuid "07c6d643-11c5-5155-8bbd-0dada6a8fa5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271519}] :question/id #uuid "dc87eb6a-695f-5bbf-80b7-7a8552f10296" :question/math-academy-id "q-140606" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+3x-2,$ then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{4}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}+3x-2,$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $3x$ | $+$ | $11$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}+3x-2\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{4}\\,\\,\\,}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{4}$ | $+$ | $3{x}^{3}$ | $-$ | $2{x}^{2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $-$ | $3{x}^{3}$ | $+$ | $2{x}^{2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $-$ | $3{x}^{3}$ | $-$ | $9{x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $6x$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $11{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $6x$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $11{x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $33x$ | $-$ | $22$ |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  | $-$ | $39x$ | $+$ | $22$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{4}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4} & =q(x)p(x)+(-39x+22),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{2}-3x+11.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=q(A)p(A)+(-39A+22I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & =q(A)p(A)+(-39A+22I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-39A+22I) \\\\  & =-39A+22I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d53194d-f90b-5604-9f95-07a29bdc2122" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7A+6I" :d