d align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$4{x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$16{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$12x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$13{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$12x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$13{x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$52x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$39$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$40x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$39$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{4}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{4} & =q(x)p(x)+(-40x-39),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{2}-4x+13.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=q(A)p(A)+(-40A-39I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & =q(A)p(A)+(-40A-39I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-40A-39I) \\\\  & =-40A-39I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326709 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "015e6485-5574-5b4c-958f-69b35790a368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16A-12I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323983} {:answer/id #uuid "1d0ef039-58a5-5609-907d-367090633d2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2A+I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324214} {:answer/id #uuid "305fc3c9-53bb-5c71-ac96-58831b482a97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A+16I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324359} {:answer/id #uuid "903e3ac2-73e8-502b-8fdf-7f4a11699ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12A-16I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325197} {:answer/id #uuid "b8a34ccb-fc36-580d-8821-fd8a627ce31a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2A+6I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12A+16I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324359} :answer-field/id #uuid "7692669f-8907-55a4-9e55-e1903c172c51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326433}] :question/id #uuid "5dab1449-918f-5266-bda4-eff0de55f52e" :question/math-academy-id "q-38705" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-2x-8,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-2x-8,$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,x$ | $+$ | $2$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-2x-8\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\,\\,}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | $-$ | $2{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $8x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | $2{x}^{2}$ | $+$ | $8x$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  | $2{x}^{2}$ | $-$ | $4x$ | $-$ | $16$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  | $12x$ | $+$ | $16$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(12x+16),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+2.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(12A+16I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(12A+16I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(12A+16I) \\\\  & =12A+16I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354448 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dadc6e-37e2-586e-a762-b4874076a22b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20A+21I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351603} {:answer/id #uuid "341e8f60-2c2f-5139-b327-47e278c2e00e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20A-21I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352054} {:answer/id #uuid "67808fb2-87cd-5157-a1e0-94315005596d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352488} {:answer/id #uuid "a32d7b40-8537-52c2-946a-2c71554d7a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A-20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352961} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3590d8-8a17-530d-9efd-1e18f0a866be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21A+20I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353325} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ced7d20-506d-5fe9-bbfe-309a56bbc614" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353838}] :question/id #uuid "62f9e5ba-0775-5b99-88ac-c3c5c53cda55" :question/math-academy-id "q-85931" :question/problem "If $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$ with characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ then ${A}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's divide the polynomial $f(x)={x}^{3}$ by characteristic polynomial $p(x)={x}^{2}-x-20,$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-x-20\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"9\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{3}\\phantom{|}\\,\\,}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$21x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$20$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write ${x}^{3}$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3} & =q(x)p(x)+(21x+20),\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)=x+1.$  Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\n{A}^{3}=q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I).\n$$\n\nNow, according to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{3} & =q(A)p(A)+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(21A+20I) \\\\  & =21A+20I.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c632238-e62f-5f74-b0da-ba8a2b7c7882" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & 0 \\\\ 72 & -27\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351821} {:answer/id #uuid "470c7209-55c8-5c45-abce-7fe3f84f4c6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & 27 \\\\ 0 & -72\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352224} {:answer/id #uuid "5e13d16b-8e89-589c-b83e-8c447ea31fb4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}27 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352401} {:answer/id #uuid "ad3d6b3f-3399-57a6-94b9-b1ab92b58f8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353035} {:answer/id #uuid "dd1b1292-04d5-5403-8881-a67fccaa7676" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}21 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353035} :answer-field/id #uuid "af398d18-f5a4-5a12-bc2f-96080c170593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354125}] :question/id #uuid "e1de5236-83e9-5753-abb0-71abaf264e50" :question/math-academy-id "q-85993" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{21}-16{x}^{19}+6x-3$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(4-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{19}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-16\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{21}\\,-\\,16{x}^{19}\\,+\\,6x\\,\\,-\\,\\,3\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{21}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$16{x}^{19}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$6x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(6x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{19}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(6A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(6A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(6A-3I) \\\\  & =6A-3I \\\\  & =6\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -24\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}21 & 72 \\\\ 0 & -27\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d95a80-3f16-57c4-aa0e-d7a0b263509f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392149} {:answer/id #uuid "7ade6fcc-fefb-5c26-9596-732bb7e6456e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -24 \\\\ 8 & -16\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392150} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8f35b7-246a-5615-af02-78cc8b431c3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392151} {:answer/id #uuid "bf93252a-5145-5f3e-a1e5-9eed34f606e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}16 & -25 \\\\ 18 & -42\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392152} {:answer/id #uuid "46d0fa8b-a3e4-5c81-b011-49838b661fc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}40 & 24 \\\\ -70 & -44\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392151} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a7442f8-2e08-50f7-921a-87fb338cdbdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392148}] :question/id #uuid "df379c8f-bbed-5154-8e34-f7aedf45ba74" :question/math-academy-id "q-37844" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{12}-4{x}^{10}+{x}^{3}-2x-3$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =det(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}14-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(14-\\lambda )(-14-\\lambda )+192 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{10}$ | $+$ | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-4\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{12}-4{x}^{10}+{x}^{3}-2x-3}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{12}$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{10}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,2x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3$ |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,4x$ |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  | $\\,\\,2x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(2x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{10}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =2A-3I \\\\  & =2\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}28 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392218 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de6c8aef-a70b-571d-ad06-c343dc69c199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 40 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392220} {:answer/id #uuid "cb7c199c-9d40-5982-8cd7-d65d993b6a6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 22 \\\\ -42 & 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392221} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad98495-909a-50b7-aa42-65cbbef7dca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & 0 \\\\ 40 & -22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392222} {:answer/id #uuid "862263ee-5ba6-55a2-96fe-c5e3f12585cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 40 \\\\ 0 & 20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392223} {:answer/id #uuid "bec74d34-14b4-582b-b3b2-0b5244b0f153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392224}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392224} :answer-field/id #uuid "b597e5da-93f2-5924-a068-9852635bdc5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392219}] :question/id #uuid "6884fbdf-c141-559a-9c69-73ca1eb1083a" :question/math-academy-id "q-38727" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{23}-25{x}^{21}-4x+2$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda ):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(5-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-25\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{23}\\,-\\,25{x}^{21}\\,-\\,4x\\,+\\,2}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{23}$ | $-$ | $25{x}^{21}$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | $-$ | $4x$ | $+$ | $2$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-4x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{21}.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-4A+2I) \\\\  & =-4A+2I \\\\  & =-4\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 10 & -5\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-20 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 20\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-18 & 0 \\\\ -40 & 22\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee48dc36-244e-5623-8162-9e5def5de475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -22 \\\\ 6 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392227} {:answer/id #uuid "4e10d15f-edfd-50e4-802f-39336ec76684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392228} {:answer/id #uuid "7b98b20b-4948-5630-912d-d10854621cc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392229} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce0307-f7b7-5df0-93a8-a3b0f9edcea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -22 \\\\ 18 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392230} {:answer/id #uuid "52829169-8b9a-5477-a7ca-27875b4c0680" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-22 & -6 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392229} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2234961-7a5f-5c89-bdd3-f09c2cf9ab03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392226}] :question/id #uuid "4c6e1cb3-d3e5-5ac7-9b61-9f6c0c45ae57" :question/math-academy-id "q-38728" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand $f(x)={x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(6-\\lambda )(-6-\\lambda )+33 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"left\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{2}-3\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"left\" colspan=\"7\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{15}-3{x}^{13}+{x}^{3}-5x+6\\phantom{|}}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{15}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,-$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{13}$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,5x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,3x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$-\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,2x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,+$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"20\" width=\"20\">$\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,6$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(-2x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{13}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(-2A+6I) \\\\  & =-2A+6I \\\\  & =-2\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 11 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}+6\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & -22 \\\\ 6 & 18\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial Using the Cayley-Hamilton Theorem"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124552 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124361 :question/id #uuid "95b44b17-b796-51eb-93dd-4ee4b2e5c3f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5894" :question/problem "Given that ![](images/25/25c8dd8e95095754a68305847645f68c6e872e9049f5062177bbac4d2fcd1164.svg) find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda),$ i.e., the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1+\\lambda_2 = \\textrm{tr}(A)= 9+(-6)=3.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87febdb4-5f54-5aff-b84a-1b05359d6b57" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c5a4bd0-9207-5164-99ac-2de3ca0280de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324083} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a7838e-204c-5871-b689-275e3a735c36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325359} {:answer/id #uuid "aed31d5a-090c-5d5a-844a-e2b0f7c1969f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325456} {:answer/id #uuid "fc64c809-216a-5942-a43f-e7a646bbe442" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326191} {:answer/id #uuid "fd96233a-e44f-51e2-aa25-ad93b0ae4ba4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325359} :answer-field/id #uuid "35e86269-599b-58dd-94b0-99c87d06a4ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326310}] :question/id #uuid "7f0cac47-d84c-5a80-b1f4-a28ee45248f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-38720" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & 7 \\\\ 9 & 3\\end{bmatrix},$ find the sum of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the sum of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the trace of $A.$ \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}=\\text{tr}(A)=-12+3=-9.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125141 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c7626ec-5cdf-5183-920c-f615785a0c47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123447} {:answer/id #uuid "b4168450-826c-5d6f-87df-97fac24fbe08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123448} {:answer/id #uuid "d3835a1d-1d0e-55ab-b5fd-050dd5742e1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123449} {:answer/id #uuid "0bd25f67-3b58-5e3d-a82e-896e9d4fd2d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123450} {:answer/id #uuid "637a2fa6-0b06-55fc-aaf1-13e03d850dfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123447} :answer-field/id #uuid "3734faa8-d4ad-5237-863b-7669bf2a5f3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123446}] :question/id #uuid "686a322b-e1a0-51fa-9c41-edfcff1a5f49" :question/math-academy-id "q-38726" :question/problem "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-14 & -2 \\\\ 71 & 10\\end{bmatrix},$ find the product of the eigenvalues of $A.$" :question/worked-solution "The characteristic polynomial of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & ={\\lambda }^{2}-\\text{tr}(A)\\lambda +\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using Vieta's Formulas, we have that the roots of $p(\\lambda ),$ i.e. the eigenvalues of $A,$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{tr}(A) \\\\ {\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} &=\\text{det}(A).\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the product of the eigenvalues of $A$ is equal to the determinant of $A.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }_{1}\\cdot {\\lambda }_{2} & =det(A) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & -2 \\\\ 71 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-14)\\cdot 10-(-2)\\cdot 71 \\\\  & =-140+142 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07145787-a560-513d-aa3e-4cd4fbfc2c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269333} {:answer/id #uuid "2e70d757-8dbc-5b1e-8d56-1c0b91cd3cb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269687} {:answer/id #uuid "581ab64f-1b42-5217-847e-d9a9da445be6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270047} {:answer/id #uuid "6fad9401-cd4e-5fd