b2d4f0ea158" :question/math-academy-id "q-127043" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ y &=5-4t \\\\ z &=2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}t-2 \\\\ 5-4t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{7}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}t \\\\ -4t \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{7}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,5,\\frac{1}{7})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290397 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "035e9ffe-6bfe-5868-8fc3-1b38cc3fb30d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288054} {:answer/id #uuid "0534d258-d4db-5214-ad61-90fe2aa10108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288069} {:answer/id #uuid "34e32f9f-1892-544b-b4bf-78a9fbebf15c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288384} {:answer/id #uuid "978239d8-2649-5735-89d8-75ed494ec4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answe