/math-academy-id "q-70716" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2t+1 \\\\ y &=3-t \\\\ z &=t+2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2t+1 \\\\ 3-t \\\\ t+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2t \\\\ -t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,3,2)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338812 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d380478-338b-5ff2-9781-0c093677bf18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336302} {:answer/id #uuid "4a591eee-d770-5356-a42b-bf90c80f485f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336717} {:answer/id #uuid "6951bd9e-e0a4-53a4-b3d6-c7536712e8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336967} {:answer/id #uuid "a43f0afa-3350-5e1e-9da9-5eebb6d7c5a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337526} {:answer/id #uuid "f9050578-131e-5f24-b6a7-45d858973769" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336302} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a0b933-d81e-5692-b217-85dee2f73b58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338306}] :question/id #uuid "02123ca6-2df3-5cd9-b5e3-668628ccd8e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-70721" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t-1 \\\\ y &=-t+1 \\\\ z &=-t-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}t-1 \\\\ -t+1 \\\\ -t-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-1,1,-1)$   and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0baa9adc-0a83-5fe5-87f8-5c4e0ac97527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336141} {:answer/id #uuid "28024701-5f72-5ab0-9e31-3397649aebff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336404} {:answer/id #uuid "aab3781d-c473-5d34-8ea9-e449887aa066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337571} {:answer/id #uuid "c0204792-3cc2-5b5d-9ff2-09dd0bb59a04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337736} {:answer/id #uuid "de4bb850-54a5-57fd-94e0-8038dfe97938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337571} :answer-field/id #uuid "13b9e8c1-bd8e-52f3-b8c1-df0c0eab3290" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338310}] :question/id #uuid "c7b2f573-0f30-58d3-9c3c-76267a728496" :question/math-academy-id "q-70722" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ y &=5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ z &=2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}t+1 \\\\ 5-\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t+\\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}t \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$  \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(1,5,\\frac{1}{3})$  and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186367219 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a143ea78-ce56-537f-b866-759793a41c5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367221} {:answer/id #uuid "c5482dda-f0b3-52e8-96b4-80b9ea9fda01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367222} {:answer/id #uuid "6dfd7bf4-7da6-5690-9cda-eeeda3b4ab78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367223} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7f243c-5ac3-587f-a1ba-fc834eb0f790" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367224} {:answer/id #uuid "a0430850-6ad4-5371-bd78-2e16594b48e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367222} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b725d9d-f657-5b50-9dfd-067e38a1f968" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186367220}] :question/id #uuid "ac9165e4-aa36-581e-a01d-16d28d3a58ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-127044" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5t-7 \\\\ y &=-1-10t \\\\ z &=\\frac{1}{4}t+\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5t-7 \\\\ -1-10t \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}t+\\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5t \\\\ -10t \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-7,-1,\\frac{3}{5})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398291 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cf3c8e5-3512-56d2-a0a2-0dfa613e95bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398293} {:answer/id #uuid "59b98ec9-bd61-5aaf-ab04-a002f394a95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398294} {:answer/id #uuid "67831711-2b31-5ce3-b5f6-cad1ba766d0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398295} {:answer/id #uuid "5cafd440-95d2-58ef-8f66-ee2335ffd0e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398296} {:answer/id #uuid "2f8093a4-96c1-598c-86b0-87a9d0382d52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398293} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e047565-9f5d-5870-acb5-4fc744551c00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398292}] :question/id #uuid "4fcf1fe7-fb4f-5cde-8368-06562ddf512e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127003" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-4t \\\\ y &=-7+3t \\\\ z &=9-t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-4t \\\\ -7+3t \\\\ 9-t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(5,-7,9)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398298 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "959a8a65-b40e-59ee-bd67-ee6449b6fd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398300} {:answer/id #uuid "4ad1ee9d-75ed-541c-8508-f6a936e76dc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398301} {:answer/id #uuid "153395aa-8829-5d10-a9fe-b0ab976a09b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398302} {:answer/id #uuid "013a87b6-78c1-51a8-95be-cd888bfc9e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398303} {:answer/id #uuid "5d58e882-8e08-50fe-a76c-3534a4a32901" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398303} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c75dc26-c081-5b28-b4c0-da76aae8f074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398299}] :question/id #uuid "82e0d9c4-429c-5e53-bd8d-068f50a3ec35" :question/math-academy-id "q-127033" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-3+7t \\\\ y &=5t \\\\ z &=1-5t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3+7t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 1-5t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}7t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -5t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(-3,0,1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313bb2ba-1cbe-5a55-988a-686dd9f3cfca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435062} {:answer/id #uuid "519e2e68-d953-5a17-b243-f7d7baf0d48c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435063} {:answer/id #uuid "5a986f85-269d-547a-a60f-07e7c95d8225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435064} {:answer/id #uuid "a026363f-0997-50ef-819e-7238a42e62f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435068} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9d7702-93e0-58b6-a557-5d52deb4131f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435063} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fdab432-8653-5165-9ae6-72fb1a348731" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435079}] :question/id #uuid "8744c31a-0769-5670-8154-7878dd8f3f11" :question/math-academy-id "q-70713" :question/problem "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t-2 \\\\ y &=2-3t \\\\ z &=2t-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}t-2 \\\\ 2-3t \\\\ 2t-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ \\,2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $(-2,2,-1)$  and is parallel to the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector Parallel To a Straight Line Given Parametrically"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124500 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124229 :question/id #uuid "173b99e8-d00c-57c8-995e-ba198361480e" :question/math-academy-id "e-15604" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](images/53/53386f04f4025fda6ab579113a8ecb53a19f4dc0a77903adc05bac3a71429717.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(3,3,-5)$ and $Q(1,0,-1)$. Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2t \\\\ -3t \\\\ 4t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-2t \\\\ 3-3t \\\\ -5+4t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-2t \\\\ y &=3-3t \\\\ z &=-5+4t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "debd4ccc-de40-55a6-9236-9bf9fff0bdb1" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b3abd30-091f-5e43-9e98-d95df81bb908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5t \\\\ y &=-10t \\\\ z &=2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288206} {:answer/id #uuid "2070aff5-0562-58d4-85b5-f49f1b64cdb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-6+5t \\\\ y &=-2-10t \\\\ z &=1+2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288240} {:answer/id #uuid "525cacca-6a59-5b07-a7e1-04907a9d42e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288603} {:answer/id #uuid "91bc8745-b2c9-575a-855d-6c8a97b7985a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-6t \\\\ y &=-10-2t \\\\ z &=2+t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289012} {:answer/id #uuid "db1a7ed9-4e4b-5f36-9a90-d5b14ccb9b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-6t \\\\ y &=-2t \\\\ z &=t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-6t \\\\ y &=-10-2t \\\\ z &=2+t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289012} :answer-field/id #uuid "a652ecee-0b3d-5881-96ae-ac8c0f2eeb7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290102}] :question/id #uuid "8d475564-a068-5f4f-ac3d-e39d879d093e" :question/math-academy-id "q-22295" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the straight line that passes through $P(5,-10,2)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨-6,-2,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, the vector equation of the line is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-6t \\\\ -2t \\\\ t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-6t \\\\ -10-2t \\\\ 2+t\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-6t \\\\ y &=-10-2t \\\\ z &=2+t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124950 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2928ac02-e877-5128-98e3-26452f115ff1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=t \\\\ y &=4t \\\\ z &=-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321466} {:answer/id #uuid "50955bcb-ad2f-567e-9725-c610ec676230" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4+t \\\\ y &=-1+4t \\\\ z &=2-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321778} {:answer/id #uuid "50a16e49-f51b-55d8-835c-20279802c311" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5+t \\\\ y &=3+4t \\\\ z &=-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321779} {:answer/id #uuid "96b3b570-f520-545f-a364-ba388699f468" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+4t \\\\ y &=4-t \\\\ z &=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322351} {:answer/id #uuid "d53ec0a4-ed61-5b6e-9858-26afcffa7811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4t \\\\ y &=-t \\\\ z &=2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+4t \\\\ y &=4-t \\\\ z &=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322351} :answer-field/id #uuid "9436eea8-a0ed-5283-ad6d-0b406bf7e409" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323457}] :question/id #uuid "b3a37d06-4a0c-5126-bd3b-fbb999a13c7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36026" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(1,4,-2)$ and $Q(5,3,0).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4t \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+4t \\\\ 4-t \\\\ -2+2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=1+4t \\\\ y &=4-t \\\\ z &=-2+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262695 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05138d70-95c1-5979-b58d-e293bc770f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-4+3t \\\\ y &=-3-2t \\\\ z &=4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422929} {:answer/id #uuid "90ed5060-8eb2-5907-9d5e-81459c8f8c02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-2t \\\\ y &=-5-2t \\\\ z &=2+3t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422930} {:answer/id #uuid "b6cefd44-c970-5d19-8f31-e184862531ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+t \\\\ y &=-5+3t \\\\ z &=4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422931} {:answer/id #uuid "b7014cb4-4b9b-5046-a88f-19f20b69fb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=5-2t \\\\ z &=-4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422932} {:answer/id #uuid "cac3e014-58d3-578a-97e4-18352d84f826" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=-5+2t \\\\ z &=-4+2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422933}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+t \\\\ y &=-5+3t \\\\ z &=4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422931} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9b1116d-ce1c-52d6-8302-1b2568c8f6a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262461}] :question/id #uuid "198cf240-fd0a-5616-aefd-68b43c60564e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127046" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(2,-5,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 3t \\\\ -2t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2+t \\\\ -5+3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+t \\\\ y &=-5+3t \\\\ z &=4-2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b361ad2-8c81-5c56-ab22-d321710878ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5+4t \\\\ y &=-3-5t \\\\ z &=5-4t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260255} {:answer/id #uuid "542bfdf7-a978-50d6-93f3-216a6b571ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+5t \\\\ y &=-3+4t \\\\ z &=5+4t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260585} {:answer/id #uuid "8efc609a-167c-5f9d-a990-da33c49c67b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+4t \\\\ y &=-3+5t \\\\ z &=5-4t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261121} {:answer/id #uuid "97eb44f4-b098-5fbc-a732-69400bdeb454" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+2t \\\\ y &=-2+4t \\\\ z &=4-3t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261192} {:answer/id #uuid "bd790227-d13d-5c73-9660-24cd22e1f3f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+4t \\\\ y &=3+5t \\\\ z &=-5+2t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+4t \\\\ y &=-3+5t \\\\ z &=5-4t\\end{aligned}\\right." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261121} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b3dad8-8449-518a-8d59-6ac30b293d52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262213}] :question/id #uuid "a6414901-e420-59fa-9f01-37ad745b6f9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127048" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line that passes through the points $P(3,-3,5)$ and $Q(7,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4t \\\\ 5t \\\\ -4t\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3+4t \\\\ -3+5t \\\\ 5-4t\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3+4t \\\\ y &=-3+5t \\\\ z &=5-4t\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262703 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answ